0,Why does the text suggest that ToT's higher cost may be justified despite requiring significantly more computations than CoT?,Vanilla_RAG,qwen,deepseek,Reasoning,medium,CONCEPT,1,DEFAULT,-1.0,0.1644,0.9231,0.2791,0,10.0,0.0,0.0,8.1,0.0009,"The text suggests ToT’s higher cost is justified because it achieves significantly higher success rates than CoT—even outperforming the *best of 100 independent CoT trials* (74% vs. 49% on Game of 24)—especially on tasks requiring deliberate, multi-step reasoning where CoT struggles. Additionally, ToT enables performance–cost tradeoffs (e.g., adjusting beam size, prompting style, or model choice) and remains effective even with weaker models like GPT-3.5, offering robustness and flexibility that justify the added computational expense for hard reasoning tasks.",ok,"But the performance of ToT is better than best of 100 independent CoT
