Knowledge-Augmented Encoder
Given an input x and
a retrieved document z, the knowledge-augmented encoder
deﬁnes p(y | z, x). We join x and z into a single sequence
that we feed into a Transformer (distinct from the one used
in the retriever).
This allows us to perform rich cross-
attention between x and z before predicting y. See Figure 1
for a concrete example.
