Math and Science Datasets Generation Details
Math Dataset.
Our Math dataset consists of 50K problem-solution pairs which are generated as
follows:
1. We ask GPT4 to generate 25 math topics.
2. We then ask GPT4 to generate 25 subtopics relevant to each of the previously generated 25
topics.
3. For each (topic,subtopic) pair we generate and solve 80 problems using GPT4.
Science Dataset.
The same recipe is used to generate the Science dataset which consists of 20K
Physics problem-solution pairs, 20K Biology problem-solution pairs, and 20K Chemistry problem-
solution pairs all generated and solved by GPT4. Similar to Math dataset we generate 25 topics
and 25 subtopics for each topic, however, the number of problems per (topic,subtopic) pair is 32
problems yielding the 20K problem-solution pairs per subject (Physics, Biology, and Chemistry).
This is summarized in Table 4.
